:[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PolicyResponse"}],"title":"PolicyResponse","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/policyresponse","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET"},{"type":"text","text":" response: the stored policy plus the unknown-AAGUID action it currently "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"resolves to","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unknown_aaguid"},{"type":"text","text":" is nullable, where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" means “use this mode’s default” (deny under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direct_required"},{"type":"text","text":", allow otherwise). A client that only saw the stored "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would have to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-derive that rule itself to display what the policy actually does — and a security rule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implemented twice is a security rule that will eventually disagree with itself. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server resolves it once, here, and reports both: the admin’s stored intent and its effect."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PolicyResponse/encode(to:)":{"title":"encode(to:)","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PolicyResponse\/encode(to:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/policyresponse\/encode(to:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"encode","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7EncoderP"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access